Runtime dependency
------------------

libheif-js 1.23.5 (LGPL-3.0)
  https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js
  A WebAssembly build of libheif (https://github.com/strukturag/libheif)
  and libde265 (https://github.com/strukturag/libde265), both LGPL-3.0,
  used to decode HEIC and HEIF images.

  This library is NOT covered by Pikado's MIT licence. It ships as the npm
  package's own file, unmodified, as a separate asset that is loaded by URL
  only when a HEIC file is opened (src/io/heif-read.js), so it can be
  replaced with any compatible build. Its source is in the three
  repositories above. The GNU Lesser General Public License 3.0 and the GNU
  General Public License 3.0 it refers to are in public/licenses/ and ship
  with every build as licenses/LGPL-3.0.txt and licenses/GPL-3.0.txt.

